Z||000000||Songman||10-03-2000||11:56 PM||||Monkeyman, I saw in another post that you use Windows ME at home. What do you think of it?<P>I had installed W2000 on my computer and loved the speed but lost support for my TV card, scanner, and all of my games. Changed to ME and now everything works but it crawls. Have you found the same thing?||||reg||5
Z||000001||whamel||10-04-2000||09:32 AM||||ME works okay for me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The system I have it on is a dual 450 PII with 256 Meg of RAM, and ATI all in wonder video capture card, 2 28 gig drives.  I had some problems on some older systems before (my 350Mhz laptop dragged) while running the beta's, but they cleared up for me in the release.  <BR>One thing I have found is that after it's up for a while it seems to have trouble releasing resources.  For example - my system has been up for 10 days, I'm using quite a bit more memory and system resources than I feel I should be.  If you want to take this to e-mail and give me more details, maybe I can help you out.<BR>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||10-04-2000||08:40 PM||||I did not think that ME supported dual processors. But then again, I have not been looking at it very much either. Where can I find more info on it? My wife's computer is a dual Pro, but I never installed the second processor because she did not like NT for everyday use.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||10-05-2000||01:07 AM|||| <A HREF="http://microsoft.com/WindowsMe/" TARGET=_blank>http://microsoft.com/WindowsMe/</A> <BR>is the basic ME info page...<BR> <A HREF="http://support.microsoft.com/support/kb/articles/Q193/6/45.ASP?LN=EN-US&SD=SO&FR=0" TARGET=_blank>http://support.microsoft.com/support/kb/articles/Q193/6/45.ASP?LN=EN-US&SD=SO&FR=0</A> <BR>states that W95/98/ME will only use one processor even if installed on a dual processor machine. W2000 was great for me and not difficult to setup and use at all. Once more suppliers get drivers working for it I will probably go back to it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||whamel||10-05-2000||09:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, lucidatypewriter">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>I did not think that ME supported dual processors. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey - I never said this was the only operating system installed on the computer.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I have 6 or 7 of them loaded up on this one for testing.<BR>Wade||||reg||1
